  "body": "**Blocked by:** none\n\n## Context\n\nPR #356 (`registry.ts`) flagged that `ModuleRegistry.loadModule` calls\n`loadModuleCatalogs(path)` (async file I/O) before `assertExportsExist` and\n`assertDataMigrationsReferenceOwnDatabases` (pure synchronous checks over the\nalready-parsed manifest). When a module fails either synchronous check, the catalog\nfile reads that already ran are wasted work — the module load will be rejected\nregardless of what's on disk.\n\n## Task\n\nIn `backend/packages/module-registry/src/registry.ts`'s `loadModule` method, reorder\nthe calls so `assertExportsExist(path, manifest, imported)` and\n`assertDataMigrationsReferenceOwnDatabases(path, manifest)` run before\n`loadModuleCatalogs(path)`. `assertCatalogKeysAvailable` still runs after\n`loadModuleCatalogs` since it needs the loaded catalogs. No other call in this\nsequence is reordered.\n\n## Touches\n\n- backend/packages/module-registry/src/registry.ts (`loadModule`)\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Reordering the four calls named above so the two synchronous checks precede the\n  catalog load.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Any other check or ordering in `loadModule`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Loading a module whose manifest fails `assertExportsExist` throws that error\n  without `loadModuleCatalogs` having been called (observable via a spy on the\n  catalog loader in a test).\n- Loading a module whose manifest fails `assertDataMigrationsReferenceOwnDatabases`\n  throws that error without `loadModuleCatalogs` having been called.\n- Loading a valid module still succeeds and its catalogs are loaded and committed as\n  before.\n\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=356 key=bb9c61e34f -->",
